ENTRY            D1094   20260525   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D1094001   20260525   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 11         43
TITLE      Gamma ray production of 7Li and 19F from
            proton-induced nuclear reactions in the energy range
            of 700-2730 keV
AUTHOR     (H.Taghipour Aslani, A.Jokar,
            A.A.Mehmandoost-Khajeh-DaD, H.Rafi-Kheiri)
INSTITUTE  (3IRNNRT)
           (3IRNIRN) University of Sistan and Baluchestan, Zahedan
           (3RUMRUM) Extreme Light Infrastructure Nuclear Physics
            (IFIN-HN), Magurele
REFERENCE  (J,EPJ/A,62,57,2026)
FACILITY   (VDG,3IRNNRT) 3 MV Van de Graaff accelerator
SAMPLE     Two LiF targets with natural isotopic composition
            were prepared using the physical vapor deposition
            technique by evaporating high-purity anhydrous LiF
            powder onto self-supporting Ag and C layer.
           For the LiF/Ag target, a self-supporting Ag layer with
            a thickness of (1235+/-50)x10**15 atom/cm2 and an area
            of 65 mm2.
           For the Au/LiF/C target, the self-supporting C layer
            consisted of a diamond-like carbon (DLC) film with a
            nominal thickness of 100 ug/cm2. A thin Au film was
            deposited onto the LiF layer.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) P-type detector with a 213 cm3 crystal placed at
            90 degree relative to the beam axis, nominal
            efficiency of 50% and resolution of ~4 keV for
            1.33 MeV gamma-ray from a 60Co source.
           (SI) Ion-implanted Si detector (25 mm2 area, 300 um
            active depth) 30 keV energy resolution was placed at a
            backward angle of 165 degree for the detection of
            scattered particles.
ANALYSIS   (NTRTH) Rutherford-scattered protons from Ag(or Au)
            were used to determine the number of incident protons.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-SYS) Systematic uncertainty
           (ERR-S) Statistical uncertainties
           (ERR-1) HPGe detector efficiency  (5%)
           (ERR-2) The number of target nuclei (7%)
           (ERR-3) The elastic scattered proton yield (1%)
           (ERR-4,,1.) Rutherford cross section for p+Ag/Au (<1%)
           (ERR-5) Particle detector solid angle (2%)
           (ERR-6) Beam energy (0.2%)
STATUS     (APRVD) Proof-read by A.Jokar (2026-05-26)
HISTORY    (20260524R) VT. Data received from A.Jokar for IBANDL
           (20260525C) VT
ENDBIB              43
COMMON               6          3
ANG        ERR-1      ERR-2      ERR-3      ERR-5      ERR-6
ADEG       PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT
        90.         5.         7.         1.         2.        0.2
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           50
SUBENT        D1094002   20260525   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                  2          3
REACTION   (9-F-19(P,INL)9-F-19,PAR,DA,G)
STATUS     (TABLE,,H.Taghipour Aslani+,J,EPJ/A,62,57,2026)
            Figures 6,7,8. Converted by R33toX4 from R33 files.
ENDBIB               3
